    {
      "id": 129,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        1774.2726969838268,
        1017.7846988353625
      ],
      "size": [
        493.82589659667065,
        634.3277316727231
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 6,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Model Links\n\nMore FLUX.2 [klein] variants (9B, base, BF16): [ComfyUI FLUX.2 [klein] tutorial](https://docs.comfy.org/tutorials/flux/flux-2-klein)\n\n**diffusion_models**\n\n- [flux-2-klein-4b-fp8.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/FLUX.2-klein-4b-fp8/resolve/main/flux-2-klein-4b-fp8.safetensors)\n\n**text_encoders**\n\n- [qwen_3_4b.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/flux2-klein-4B/resolve/main/split_files/text_encoders/qwen_3_4b.safetensors)\n\n**latent upscaler** (downloaded automatically on first use)\n\n- [steppe_flux_2_200M_1step.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/TensorForger/Steppe-Flux.2/resolve/main/steppe_flux_2_200M_1step.safetensors)\n\n**vae**\n\n- [flux2-vae.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/flux2-dev/resolve/main/split_files/vae/flux2-vae.safetensors)\n\n## Model Storage Location\n\n```\n📂 ComfyUI/\n├── 📂 models/\n│   ├── 📂 diffusion_models/\n│   │   └── flux-2-klein-4b-fp8.safetensors\n│   ├── 📂 text_encoders/\n│   │   └── qwen_3_4b.safetensors\n│   ├── 📂 latent_upscale_models/\n│   │   └── steppe_flux_2_200M_1step.safetensors\n│   └── 📂 vae/\n│       └── flux2-vae.safetensors\n```\n\n## Steppe\n\n- Each **Steppe Upscale Latent** node doubles the resolution of the FLUX.2 latent: 896x512 → 1792x1024 → 3584x2048. No second sampling pass, no prompt.\n- Works with every FLUX.2 VAE model: FLUX.2 [dev], FLUX.2 [klein] and MOSS-Image.\n- `hff` (0...1, default 0.9) sets the amount of fine detail; `-1` lets the model choose.\n- For large outputs use `VAE Decode (Tiled)` if the decode runs out of memory.\n\n## Custom Nodes\n\n- [ComfyUI-Steppe](https://github.com/TensorForger/ComfyUI-Steppe)\n- [rgthree-comfy](https://github.com/rgthree/rgthree-comfy): Image Comparer, the output node of this workflow (or replace it with two `Save Image` nodes)\n"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## Model Links\n\nMore FLUX.2 [klein] variants (9B, base, BF16): [ComfyUI FLUX.2 [klein] tutorial](https://docs.comfy.org/tutorials/flux/flux-2-klein)\n\n**diffusion_models**\n\n- [flux-2-klein-4b-fp8.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/FLUX.2-klein-4b-fp8/resolve/main/flux-2-klein-4b-fp8.safetensors)\n\n**text_encoders**\n\n- [qwen_3_4b.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/flux2-klein-4B/resolve/main/split_files/text_encoders/qwen_3_4b.safetensors)\n\n**latent upscaler** (downloaded automatically on first use)\n\n- [steppe_flux_2_200M_1step.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/TensorForger/Steppe-Flux.2/resolve/main/steppe_flux_2_200M_1step.safetensors)\n\n**vae**\n\n- [flux2-vae.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/flux2-dev/resolve/main/split_files/vae/flux2-vae.safetensors)\n\n## Model Storage Location\n\n```\n📂 ComfyUI/\n├── 📂 models/\n│   ├── 📂 diffusion_models/\n│   │   └── flux-2-klein-4b-fp8.safetensors\n│   ├── 📂 text_encoders/\n│   │   └── qwen_3_4b.safetensors\n│   ├── 📂 latent_upscale_models/\n│   │   └── steppe_flux_2_200M_1step.safetensors\n│   └── 📂 vae/\n│       └── flux2-vae.safetensors\n```\n\n## Steppe\n\n- Each **Steppe Upscale Latent** node doubles the resolution of the FLUX.2 latent: 896x512 → 1792x1024 → 3584x2048. No second sampling pass, no prompt.\n- Works with every FLUX.2 VAE model: FLUX.2 [dev], FLUX.2 [klein] and MOSS-Image.\n- `hff` (0...1, default 0.9) sets the amount of fine detail; `-1` lets the model choose.\n- For large outputs use `VAE Decode (Tiled)` if the decode runs out of memory.\n\n## Custom Nodes\n\n- [ComfyUI-Steppe](https://github.com/TensorForger/ComfyUI-Steppe)\n- [rgthree-comfy](https://github.com/rgthree/rgthree-comfy): Image Comparer, the output node of this workflow (or replace it with two `Save Image` nodes)\n"
      },
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
